<p>Here I used an iOS 11+ API, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">maskedCorners</code>, which can round corners in different directions. Many people wonder whether setting the corner radius and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">masksToBounds</code> easily triggers offscreen rendering and causes extra overhead. If you have this question, please refer to my article on <a href="https://www.sunyazhou.com/2018/05/HowToCreateTopBottomRoundedCornersForViews/">rounding different corners of a UIView</a>.</p>

